        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy an 8,000 watt generator if your outage list includes a well pump or a furnace and a window AC, and you can install a 30-amp inlet and transfer switch. It is the largest size that connection can use, and it runs the loads that matter together instead of in rotation. The Westinghouse WGen7500DFc is the best all-round choice, the DuroMax XP9500iH is the best on propane and the quietest to live with, and the WEN DF8000X is the budget way in if your motor loads are modest.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If your list stops at the fridge and the router, buy smaller. If it includes central air, buy bigger and change to a 50-amp connection first. Either way, plan the fuel: about 10 gallons of gasoline or 60 pounds of propane a day.
          </p>
